  "helpTitle": "How to play",
  "helpReplay": "Show the tutorial again",
  "help_goal_t": "Goal",
  "help_goal": "Grandpa is always late for Grandma's afternoon tea, and he wants the one clock that is never wrong: Chronos, the god of time — the last and most expensive clock in the game. Get him and the story goes on.\nThe way there: hit 5.00, collect Ticks, and spend them on clocks that earn for you.",
  "help_tiki_t": "Ticks",
  "help_tiki": "Ticks are the game's currency. At the top of the screen:\n• the big number — your Ticks\n• below it — how many you gain per second\n• \"5.00 = +…\" — what a hit on exactly 5.00 pays\nYou spend Ticks in the shop at the bottom: on clocks and skills.",
  "help_clocks_t": "Clocks",
  "help_clocks": "Clocks play rounds for you (the bubbles beside the dial show their results) and give Ticks every second — even while the game is closed, up to a time limit.\n• Buying a clock reveals the next one: pricier and stronger.\n• The number on the icon — how many you own.\n• Each extra copy of the same clock costs a bit more.\n• ×1, ×10, ×100, MAX — how many you buy at once.",
  "help_upgrades_t": "Clock bonuses",
  "help_upgrades": "The bar under a clock shows how many more you need for the next step, e.g. \"20/40 → ×2\". At each step all clocks of that kind earn that many times more, for good.\n• First clocks: steps at 10, 20, 40… and ×2.\n• Pricier clocks: lower steps, smaller multipliers.\nSynergy: 25 each of two matching clocks (e.g. Grandpa and Grandma) boosts both.",
  "help_skills_t": "Skills",
  "help_skills": "Skills boost your own hits — not the clocks. Among others: bigger rewards, wider grade windows and a higher multiplier.\n• Each has levels, e.g. \"Level 2/10\"; the next level costs more Ticks.\n• A new card appears as you get close to its price.\n• Tap a card to see its exact effect.",
  "help_combo_t": "Multiplier (combo)",
  "help_combo": "The multiplier next to COMBO multiplies all your payouts. A PERFECT raises it by 0.05, an exact 5.00 straight to the cap (the Combo skill raises the cap). GREAT and GOOD leave it alone.\nA CLOSE or a miss resets the multiplier. Except: a Shield charge (a skill) takes one miss; charges come back every 10 hits, counting from zero once one is used.\nThe streak — hits in a row — counts only during a \"streak\" challenge: from zero until the first miss, even one a Shield took.",
  "help_golden_t": "Golden Second",
  "help_golden": "About every 10 minutes a golden clock flies across the screen. Tapping it turns the next round golden.\nA hit in a golden round gives a random reward:\n• Frenzy (45%) — all income ×7 for 77 s\n• Lucky (45%) — Ticks worth 10 minutes of your clocks, right away\n• Hot hand (10%) — for 60 s every hit counts as PERFECT and pays ×10\nThe reward's strength depends on the grade: PERFECT 100%, GREAT 60%, GOOD 30%, a miss nothing.",
  "help_modes_t": "Toggles",
  "help_modes": "Toggles above the shop change the rules of a round. Each appears only once unlocked:\n• Blind — somewhere between 3.60 and 4.20 (a different moment each round) the digits and the ring disappear; hits pay ×3 (×4 with the Daredevil perk)\n• Second clock — two stopwatches at once; the left and right half of the screen are separate clocks\n• Auto-buyer — buys the clock you pick up to its next bonus, then turns orange and waits for your next pick",
  "help_season_t": "Events",
  "help_season": "On holidays the golden clock changes its look. The badge at the top counts two goals: holiday clocks caught (e.g. 0/5) and hits (e.g. 0/50). Both together earn a reward, and the holiday theme stays unlocked.",
  "help_prestige_t": "Time paradox",
  "help_prestige": "Once you've earned enough Ticks, the swirl at the top lights up. Rewinding time resets your Ticks, clocks and skills. In return you get:\n• Chronons — a permanent multiplier on all income; their number grows with the Ticks earned this loop\n• Shards of time — as many as Chronons; they pay for perks\nYou buy perks right after the rewind or later on the paradox screen. Chronons, Shards, perks and achievements stay.",
  "help_icons_t": "Icons at the top",
  "help_icons": "• Trophy — achievements (each: +1% income)\n• Chart — statistics\n• Dial — the stopwatch look\n• Question mark — this help\n• Gear — settings\n• Swirl — time paradox\n• Spiral — Mainsprings",
