  "chapter_1_t": "Summoned",
  "chapter_1": "*: Grandpa's garage. An altar, smoke, and the smell of cheesecake.\nchronos: Who summons me?\ngrandpa: Me. Small favour. Every day at five I need to be in the kitchen.\nchronos: You summoned the god of time to make it to tea.\ngrandpa: Afternoon tea. There's cheesecake.\ngrandma (from the kitchen): The cake's getting cold!\nchronos (freezes): Who was that?\ngrandpa: The wife.\nchronos: I'm turning time back. To that afternoon tea.\ngrandpa: And the clocks?\nchronos: The clocks won't remember. You will. And this time, no digits.",
  "@chapter_1": {
    "description": "Story script: one line per row, 'speaker (stage direction): text'. Speakers: grandpa, grandma, chronos, or * for a caption. Keep the speaker ids and the colon; translate the rest."
  },
  "chapter_2_t": "No digits",
  "chapter_2": "*: The garage. The altar. Again.\nchronos: No digits, and still on five. You can feel time.\ngrandpa: Why did you run off last time?\nchronos: Gods don't run off. Gods withdraw.\ngrandpa: Grandma asks if you'd drop by for tea.\nchronos: Gods don't drop by.\nchronos: Next lesson: time costs. From now on every second costs more.",
  "@chapter_2": {
    "description": "Story script: one line per row, 'speaker (stage direction): text'. Speakers: grandpa, grandma, chronos, or * for a caption. Keep the speaker ids and the colon; translate the rest."
  },
  "chapter_3_t": "Price hike",
  "chapter_3": "chronos: Expensive?\ngrandpa: Less than anniversary flowers. I forgot those, so it came out cheaper.\nchronos (quietly): The fourteenth of May.\ngrandpa: How do you know?\nchronos: I don't. Lucky guess.\nchronos: Next lesson: the sun stays behind a cloud. You don't get lucky with tea. You turn up for it.",
  "@chapter_3": {
    "description": "Story script: one line per row, 'speaker (stage direction): text'. Speakers: grandpa, grandma, chronos, or * for a caption. Keep the speaker ids and the colon; translate the rest."
  },
  "chapter_4_t": "The fourth cup",
  "chapter_4": "chronos: No sun, and you still made it.\nchronos: Who's the fourth cup for?\ngrandpa: Grandma always sets one too many. I don't ask. Fifty years, I don't ask.\nchronos: …\nchronos: Next lesson: one sloppy hit and you start over. That's how it is with dates.\ngrandpa: With what?\nchronos: Nothing. Turning time back.",
  "@chapter_4": {
    "description": "Story script: one line per row, 'speaker (stage direction): text'. Speakers: grandpa, grandma, chronos, or * for a caption. Keep the speaker ids and the colon; translate the rest."
  },
  "chapter_5_t": "Five seconds",
  "chapter_5": "chronos: Once in my life I stopped time for a human.\ngrandpa: For long?\nchronos: Five seconds.\ngrandpa: For whom?\nchronos: Someone running late. Running with flowers. Losing petals.\ngrandpa: What an idiot.\nchronos: Mm-hm.\nchronos: Next lesson: a sloppy hit doesn't count.",
  "@chapter_5": {
    "description": "Story script: one line per row, 'speaker (stage direction): text'. Speakers: grandpa, grandma, chronos, or * for a caption. Keep the speaker ids and the colon; translate the rest."
  },
  "chapter_6_t": "Behind the door",
  "chapter_6": "*: The kitchen. The garage door is shut.\ngrandma (to the door): I know you're in there.\nchronos (behind the door): I'm not here.\ngrandma: You haven't been here for fifty years. I still cut the cheesecake in four.\ngrandpa (whispering, to you): Who's she talking to?\nchronos: Last lesson. No sleeping. Those who sleep run late.",
  "@chapter_6": {
    "description": "Story script: one line per row, 'speaker (stage direction): text'. Speakers: grandpa, grandma, chronos, or * for a caption. Keep the speaker ids and the colon; translate the rest."
  },
  "chapter_7_t": "Five sharp",
  "chapter_7": "*: Grandma's kitchen. The clock says 4:59.\n*: The door. Grandpa. Early, for the first time ever.\ngrandma: A minute early.\ngrandpa: All by myself. No clocks.\n*: A knock. Five o'clock sharp.\nchronos: On time.\ngrandma (pours the fourth cup): Sit down.\nchronos: I don't do tea.\ngrandma: I know. Fifty years you haven't.\ngrandpa: You two know each other?\ngrandma: For five seconds. Back in seventy-four.\nchronos (sits down): …Cheesecake?",
  "@chapter_7": {
    "description": "Story script: one line per row, 'speaker (stage direction): text'. Speakers: grandpa, grandma, chronos, or * for a caption. Keep the speaker ids and the colon; translate the rest."
  },
  "help_round_t": "The round",
  "help_round": "The stopwatch counts up from zero. Tap the screen when it shows 5.00 — how close you get sets the grade:\n• exactly 5.00 (±0.010 s) — a PERFECT, a bonus of Ticks worth a few seconds of your clocks, and the full multiplier\n• PERFECT (±0.015 s) — 6 Ticks, multiplier +0.05\n• GREAT (±0.030 s) — 3 Ticks\n• GOOD (±0.050 s) — 1 Tick\n• CLOSE (±0.150 s) — a small consolation, the multiplier is lost\nAnything further is a miss. A tap more than a second before 5.00 doesn't count. Skills widen the grade windows (except \"exactly 5.00\").",
  "help_res_t": "Resources",
  "help_res_tiki": "Ticks — currency: clocks and skills",
  "help_res_chronon": "Chronons — a permanent income multiplier from the paradox",
  "help_res_shard": "Shards of time — the currency of perks",
  "help_res_spring": "Mainsprings — clock mastery",
  "helpLocked": "Keep playing to unlock new mechanics",
  "notificationAskBody": "Your clocks earn while the game is closed — but only up to a time limit. We'll tell you when they reach it and remind you of the daily bonus. Two notifications at most, never at night.",
  "notificationAskYes": "Yes, let me know",
  "notificationAskNo": "No, thanks",
  "prologue_t": "Prologue: Seven minutes",
  "prologue": "*: Grandma's kitchen. The table is set for four.\n*: Five o'clock. Grandpa's chair is empty.\ngrandma (hands you a stopwatch): Time him, dear.\n*: Seven minutes later.\ngrandma: Seven minutes.\ngrandpa: Impossible. My watch says five.\ngrandma: Your watch has said five for fifty years.\ngrandpa (whispering, to you): You've got a hand for the stopwatch. Takes after Grandma.\ngrandpa: Tomorrow I'll be on the dot. I just need a better clock.\ngrandma: There's only one clock that's never wrong.\ngrandpa: Chronos. I know. I've read about him.\ngrandma (looks at the fourth cup): We don't talk about him at the table.\ngrandpa (whispering, to you): But we can get him. We'll start with smaller clocks.",
