  "story_atomic_t": "Atomic clock",
  "story_atomic": "grandpa: An atomic clock. Off by a second every hundred million years.\ngrandpa: Tomorrow I'm in the kitchen at five sharp.\ngrandma: You said that about the cuckoo.\ngrandpa: The cuckoo was from a fair.\ngrandma: And the lateness?\ngrandpa: …Force of habit.",
  "@story_atomic": {
    "description": "Story script: one line per row, 'speaker (stage direction): text'. Speakers: grandpa, grandma, chronos, or * for a caption. Keep the speaker ids and the colon; translate the rest."
  },
  "story_paradox_t": "Backwards",
  "story_paradox": "*: Every clock in the garage spins backwards.\ngrandpa: It worked! We turned time back!\ngrandma (from the kitchen): Did you blow a fuse again?\nchronos (from very far away): Who's fiddling with my clocks?\ngrandpa (whispering, to you): We act like nothing happened.",
  "@story_paradox": {
    "description": "Story script: one line per row, 'speaker (stage direction): text'. Speakers: grandpa, grandma, chronos, or * for a caption. Keep the speaker ids and the colon; translate the rest."
  },
  "story_timeMachine_t": "Seventy-four",
  "story_timeMachine": "grandpa: A time machine. I'd go back to seventy-four.\ngrandma: What for?\ngrandpa: To turn up for our first date on time.\ngrandma: You did turn up on time.\ngrandpa: I ran like mad. I was sure I'd be late.\ngrandma (quietly): Someone helped you.",
  "@story_timeMachine": {
